  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 AM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nA gradual moderation in temperatures will be realized through \nthe first half of next week as the pattern shifts to an upper\nridge overhead. This ridge has impressive strength with mid- \nlevel heights in the upper couple percentile for the time of \nyear (580 dam). This, along with the blocky pattern, signifies \nthe ridge has staying power. So local area dryness should \ncontinue with only a quarter of available NBM members showing \nshowers in the Wednesday night to Thursday time. With midweek \nmoderating afternoon temperatures to around 60 this time of \nyear, we would typically be concerned about a potential fire \nweather threat (i.e. concurrent gusty southwest winds). However,\nbecause of the pattern sluggishness, the pressure gradient is \nslow to tighten so there is not an immediate signal in our \nforecast tools for overlapping anomalous winds and warmth.",
